oc=AdnJDMrbGk4xmPmyprqoaye7Cj_HhwoLcCVSaoJQ8-wfFyWS7WU48qHxI5jLenHANfE&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-iad3-2.oculuscdn.com&oh=00_AfulLEHPN555ksUXqwezo6h3AHkRNrmAzx6ZLkNmL-vOsA&oe=699DA8D5"}, {"file_name": "2 Screenshot 2560x1440.png", "id": "1219888766768995", "uri": "https://scontent-iad3-1.oculuscdn.com/v/t64.5771-25/499617762_1219888770102328_625861554141402806_n.png?_nc_cat=110&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=sYjhtrx3gSIQ7kNvwGm_MjT&_nc_oc=AdnapADDFe8UAUKV2C9XiNPJXza6LS6FUI6hnI62WtROZRa85uNP3hTOydLy9KBaJlQ&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-iad3-1.oculuscdn.com&oh=00_AftpqQMULgwarpd7II8eseaDsAczL1K304iNmcwte5ML-A&oe=699DA06F"}], "video_trailer": null, "video_trailer_thumbnail": null, "display_name": "IMVR", "keywords": ["imvr", "interactionwithnature", "longlamai", "Penan", "molong"], "long_description": "IMVR is a co-designed virtual reality experience developed in close collaboration with the Penan community of Long Lamai, Sarawak (East Malaysia).\n\nRooted in the indigenous concept of Molong, a philosophy of care, custodianship, and reciprocal relationships with nature, IMVR invites users to experience the rainforest not as an observer, but as a part of it. \n\n**What you can experience**\n\n- Explore a 3D rainforest environment inspired by the Borneo rainforest\n- Choose a living entity (Olong) and see the world from its perspective\n- Immerse yourself in authentic forest soundscapes\n- Learn about indigenous ecological values through embodied interaction\n\n**Why IMVR** \n\nIMVR fosters ecological awareness, and a deeper emotional connection with the forest (tana), through immersion, not instruction.", "short_description": "IMVR is a co-designed virtual reality experience developed with the Penan community of Long Lamai in Sarawak, Malaysia, exploring the indigenous concept of Molong and inviting users to form immersive relationships with nature."}]}, "developer_name": "Naqib Izzuddin Bin Hussien, Diana Azlyz, Tariq Zaman", "developer_privacy_policy_url": "https://github.co